# Computer Vision Projects

## Overview
This folder contains computer vision and image restoration work focused on multiscale methods, old photo restoration, and image enhancement pipelines.

## Problem
Real-world images often suffer from blur, noise, scratches, low contrast, and other degradations. This project explores classical image processing techniques to restore and enhance image quality.

## Project Focus
- Image restoration
- Multiscale pyramids
- Old photo restoration
- Enhancement and preprocessing workflows

## Methods and Tools
- Python
- Jupyter Notebook
- OpenCV
- Multiscale image processing
- Restoration pipelines

## Files
- `ImageRestoration_MultiScalePyramids.ipynb` — multiscale restoration notebook
- `old_photo_restoration.ipynb` — restoration workflow notebook
- `old_photo_restoration.pdf` — project writeup/report
- `cset03.html` — exported artifact

## Key Takeaways
- Applied multiscale image processing concepts to restoration tasks
- Explored practical tradeoffs in image enhancement and repair
- Built a foundation for low-level vision preprocessing relevant to downstream perception systems

## How to Use
1. Start with the PDF if you want a quick summary
2. Open the notebooks to inspect implementation details
3. Run notebook cells in sequence to reproduce intermediate steps
